{"qid":"Q2320005","names":["Ptolemaic Kingdom"],"title":"Ptolemaic Kingdom","endonym":null,"capsule":"The Ptolemaic Kingdom was founded by Ptolemy I Soter, one of Alexander's generals, who took Egypt as his satrapy after 323 BC and proclaimed himself king in 305 BC, establishing a Macedonian dynasty that ruled from Alexandria. At its apex under Ptolemy III Euergetes (r. 246–222 BC) it controlled Egypt, Cyrenaica, Cyprus, parts of the Levantine coast, and trading posts into the Red Sea, making Alexandria the most cosmopolitan city of the Hellenistic world. Dynastic strife, Roman interference, and territorial losses to the Seleucids and Rome progressively reduced the kingdom; Cleopatra VII's alignment with first Julius Caesar and then Mark Antony ended when Octavian's forces defeated Antony at Actium in 31 BC, and Egypt was absorbed as a Roman province in 30 BC, closing the dynasty.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Egypt proper is excellently attested through papyrological, numismatic, and administrative sources; Ptolemaic control of the Levant, Aegean islands, and Cyrenaica fluctuated and is reconstructed from diplomatic correspondence, inscriptions, and literary sources, with frontier zones carrying moderate uncertainty.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Egypt - Ptolemaic dynasty","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Egypt/Ptolemaic-dynasty"},{"label":"Britannica: Ptolemaic dynasty","url":"https://www.britannica.com/topic/Ptolemaic-dynasty"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Ptolemaic Kingdom","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ptolemaic_Kingdom"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Ptolemaic Kingdom","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Ptolemy I Soter","nativeName":"Πτολεμαῖος Α΄ Σωτήρ","roman":"Ptolemaîos I Sōtḗr","start":-305,"end":-282,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Ptolemy II Philadelphus","nativeName":"Πτολεμαῖος Β΄ Φιλάδελφος","roman":"Ptolemaîos II Philádelphos","start":-282,"end":-246,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Ptolemy III Euergetes","nativeName":"Πτολεμαῖος Γ΄ Εὐεργέτης","roman":"Ptolemaîos III Euergétēs","start":-246,"end":-222,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Ptolemy IV Philopator","nativeName":"Πτολεμαῖος Δ΄ Φιλοπάτωρ","roman":"Ptolemaîos IV Philopátōr","start":-222,"end":-204,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Ptolemy V Epiphanes","nativeName":"Πτολεμαῖος Ε΄ Ἐπιφανής","roman":"Ptolemaîos V Epiphanḗs","start":-204,"end":-180,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Ptolemy VI Philometor","nativeName":"Πτολεμαῖος ΣΤ΄ Φιλομήτωρ","roman":"Ptolemaîos VI Philomḗtōr","start":-180,"end":-145,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Cleopatra II","nativeName":"Κλεοπάτρα Β΄","roman":"Kleopátra II","start":-175,"end":-116,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Ptolemy VIII Euergetes II (Physcon)","nativeName":"Πτολεμαῖος Η΄ Εὐεργέτης","roman":"Ptolemaîos VIII Euergétēs","start":-145,"end":-116,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Cleopatra III","nativeName":"Κλεοπάτρα Γ΄","roman":"Kleopátra III","start":-116,"end":-101,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Ptolemy IX Soter II (Lathyros)","nativeName":"Πτολεμαῖος Θ΄ Σωτήρ","roman":"Ptolemaîos IX Sōtḗr","start":-116,"end":-107,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Ptolemy X Alexander I","nativeName":"Πτολεμαῖος Ι΄ Ἀλέξανδρος","roman":"Ptolemaîos X Aléxandros","start":-